```python
# ============================================================
# CONCEPT 6: HOW REQUEST-RESPONSE CYCLE WORKS
# ============================================================

# FULL FLOW for /blog/hello/ request:

# 1. Browser sends GET request to http://127.0.0.1:8000/blog/hello/

# 2. Django receives request in myproject/urls.py
#    sees 'blog/' prefix → forwards to blog/urls.py

# 3. blog/urls.py sees 'hello/' → calls hello_view(request)

# 4. hello_view runs:
def hello_view(request):
    return HttpResponse("Hello World")
    # creates HttpResponse object with "Hello World"
    # returns it to Django

# 5. Django sends HttpResponse back to browser

# 6. Browser displays "Hello World"

# request object contains:
print(request.method)   # "GET" — type of request
print(request.path)     # "/blog/hello/" — URL path
print(request.GET)      # query parameters from URL
# ?name=Ravi → request.GET = {'name': 'Ravi'}
```

